From 6a18bcc4a18a2f76562bc7902681387b7a8f2762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bensasl2 <ben@deeprey.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:35:25 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ocharts: async (off-thread) chart loader to remove
 pan/zoom decrypt lag

- Move the blocking oexserverd decrypt + SENC parse off the GUI thread into a
  single background worker (eSENCChartLoadManager); panning no longer freezes
  ~141ms/cell. The render virtuals are gated on a new m_bDataReady flag, so a
  not-yet-loaded cell shows the basemap until the worker completes + RequestRefresh.
- Split BuildRAZFromSENCFile into BuildRAZ_WorkerPhase (decrypt/parse, no ps52plib)
  and BuildRAZ_MainPhase (ps52plib LUP walk + assembly, GUI thread).
- Stage all GUI-visible metadata in ChartLoadJob and copy it to chart members on
  the GUI thread (race-free); no synchronous per-cell header round-trip.
- Lifetime: per-chart shared_ptr<JobState>; ~eSENCChart CancelAndWait blocks until
  the worker leaves the chart's phase. Expiry handled in FinishAsyncLoad; DeInit
  shuts the SENC server down before joining the worker so it cannot hang.
---
